{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI held-out compatibility finding reproduced RED before repair: direct _resolve_held_lock callers received _Disposition.IN_FLIGHT instead of historical integer 3 in both live-holder and freed-then-acquire-lost cases. The implementation worker corrected the representation boundary without seeing or editing the held-out facade tests: the helper again returns 3, while main translates that semantic state through _Disposition.IN_FLIGHT so canonical sync exits 0 and legacy routes retain exit 3 plus their exact message. Post-fix GREEN evidence: the two previously failing nodes 2/2; focused canonical/legacy/direct-engine/workflow/selection suite 85/85; make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; module remains 798/800. The CI RED is the defect-seeded mutation (the prior patchset had reintroduced the exact enum-leak mechanism); refactoring litmus passes because tests assert only observable return/exit/message behavior."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786259378817386001,"uuid":"f8e07b38-bf82-49c9-bf68-cf38577c8eb5"}